      "summary": "Wrote /workspace/impl_diffs/tp_nvshmem.md specifying the in-kernel device-NVSHMEM TP/SP all-reduce the user wants (reduction done INSIDE the persistent 1-CTA/SM megakernel, NOT a host CUDA-graph stitch). Answered the three required questions: (1) NVSHMEM is NOT installable as-is -- it is an environment gate (verified: no nvshmem.h/libs/bitcode; -DSG_HAS_NVSHMEM=1 fails at the include; loopback TU compiles clean WITHOUT the flag); user must pip install nvidia-nvshmem-cu12 or use HPC-SDK. (2) The exact device-side sequence at each of the 4 GridBarrier reduce points (anchors verbatim from model_stage_decoder_tc.cuh lines 1570-72, 1601-03, 1878-81, 1907-10): partial already in tr.local(slot) -> tr.rendezvous(bar) [GridBarrier + nvshmem_quiet + one-CTA team barrier] -> tp_allreduce_sum_fixed_order [ASCENDING-pe fp32, the A/A/A-preserving hand loop, NOT nvshmemx_float_sum_reduce] -> tr.rendezvous(bar). (3) Two-barrier nesting: GridBarrier is cross-CTA-within-GPU, nvshmem barrier is cross-GPU/grid-wide and must be entered by exactly one CTA per GPU. Apply-ready VERBATIM-OLD/NEW diffs for tp_transport.cuh (harden NvshmemTransport: add nvshmem_quiet + TP-team scoping so DP/PP replicas aren't dragged in) and parallel_config.cuh (widen CommCtx with the symmetric-heap base/stride + team pe/size) -- both compile-safe on this box behind #if SG_HAS_NVSHMEM and SingleGPU-byte-identical. Flagged honestly: the megakernel is still template <OptId Opt> only (ParConfig/CommCtx NOT yet threaded), and the operands CANNOT stay in the cudaMalloc workspace -- they must move to an nvshmem_malloc'd symmetric heap (the forced allocator change), spec'd as a ~216 MB/GPU dedicated TP-slot symmetric region."
