      ],
      "summary": "Wrote /workspace/impl_diffs/run_harness.md as apply-ready NEW-files-only spec: (1) grokking_optimizers/parallel/flagship_budget.py — pure-Python per-rank memory arithmetic mirroring the LIVE kernel scratch formulas (sg2_ws_stride<SG2Dims<>> from opt_stage_supergrok2.cuh, dec_tc_{sg2,muon,looksam,acts}_floats from fused_decoder_megakernel.cuh:502-650, SG2 9-plane state layout), and (2) tuning/flagship_distributed.py — the torchrun harness. Both Python blocks compile clean and the budget numbers were executed/verified self-consistent.\n\nKEY RESULT (computed from live formulas, not estimates): the SG2 per-CTA stride is ~91.3*Nmax floats (header said ~50). At the flagship the largest tensor is ff=dff*d=10,240,000; TP=t shrinks per-rank Nmax to Nmax/t. RECOMMENDED MESH: TP8 * DP1 * PP1 * ZeRO-3. At TP=8, per-rank Nmax=1.28M -> 10 of 11 optimizers run at nCTA=132 (one-CTA/SM, 66-68 GiB/rank); SuperGrok2 is 70.52 GiB at nCTA=132 (0.01 over the 70.5 GiB usable line) so auto_ncta() caps ONLY SG2 to nCTA=64 (40.9 GiB). All 11 saturate all 8 GPUs (TP saturates, nCTA is occupancy). TP4xDP2 and TP2xPP2xDP2 are strictly worse: ZeRO-3 shards params/state over DP but NOT the transient per-CTA workspace, so their larger Nmax forces an nCTA cap (or OOM) on EVERY opt (TP4xDP2 nCTA=132 -> 129 GiB OOM). \n\nThe harness builds the flagship TU per-rank via cpp_extension.load of mega_decoder_real_adamw_tc.cu (the same coexisting-variant build decoder_bench.py uses, never touching _ops) with the proven flagship.md layout swap (-DSG_FUSED_SM90_DECODER_LAYOUT_CUH_=1 -include decoder_flagship_layout.cuh) + -DSG_TUNED_GEMM_IMPL=1 (L3-TC) + -DSG_FLAGSHIP_TP/PP/DP/ZERO. Staged-opt scratch carved UNCONDITIONALLY (NOT SG_DEC_BENCH_LAYOUT) so the full suite runs. Seeds identically (seed_everything + same-seed flat blob, the test_distributed_step §7.1 convention), runs the in-kernel-TP fused step on real grokking data (make_data_for_task), and verifies cross-rank loss bit-eq (Δ<1e-